/-!
# The Levi decomposition of the unitary-five plane parabolic

A trace-one change of basis gives a special-unitary GL₂ section of restriction
to the marked isotropic plane. Its projective scalar kernel is the group of
fifth roots of unity for fourth-power conjugation, and its SL₂ part embeds
faithfully. `planeRadicalLevi` names the subgroup generated by this SL₂ image
and the faithful unipotent parameter image.

The unipotent image exhausts the restriction kernel and is normal in the full
projective parabolic. The quotient is GL₂ modulo scalar fifth roots, with a
faithful Levi section. Actual conjugation identifies `planeRadicalLevi` with
the unipotent--SL₂ semidirect product. Determinant modulo fifth roots makes
this subgroup normal of index three over F₁₆. The genuine action on plane
lines gives flag index seventeen. Identification with the solvable residual
requires the separate perfection argument.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*,
F.1.12(7), printed pp.263--264.
-/
